---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About Us" description="Troy Sybert on Voice of Repentance. A record of one man still walking, still learning, still turning.">
  <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
   <div class="grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,24rem)] items-start">
    <div>
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl text-vor-charcoal mb-6">About Troy and VOR</h1>
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <p>
        Modern religion has gotten very good at softening the Bible into something people can swallow at a Sunday brunch. I will not do that here. If you are going to believe the book, believe it. It has hard truths that cost something, and washing over them to keep people in the pews is its own kind of unfaithfulness. What this site offers instead is a journey. I would like you to come along, but softening the message and flattering you into it is just not my style.
      </p>
      <p>
        My name is Troy Sybert. I grew up blue-collar, the kind of blue-collar where popcorn was dinner more than once because dinner had to stretch. I am now a physician, having been trained at institutions such as the Mayo Clinic, one of the most respected medical institutions in the world. None of that arc was my doing. It was God's direction on my life, carried out through the people He put around me.
      </p>
      <p>
        My parents taught me what stability looks like by scraping it together when it would have been easier to quit. My teachers kept reinforcing, sometimes patiently and sometimes not, that hard work actually has rewards, and that a kid from nowhere can get somewhere if he doesn't stop walking. My ministers showed me that serving people is different from preaching at them, and that the first one is harder and matters more. I owe a lot to people I will not name here because the list would make the post too long. The pattern was always the same: God put someone in my path at exactly the point where I needed to be pushed, held, or corrected.
      </p>
      <p>
        Twenty years of medicine has sat me next to more human tragedy than I can describe. That work changes a person. It made me more direct, probably too direct sometimes, and it left me with a cynicism about human nature for which I do not apologize. Most of us ignore the warnings that would lengthen our lives until the last-minute emergency, and by then the options are fewer. I have watched this in exam rooms for almost three decades, and I recognize it now when I open my Bible. The same pattern that kills people slowly in the body is what scripture describes as happening in the soul. Sin crouching at the door, eager to master us, and most of us politely refusing to notice until we cannot turn away.
      </p>
      <p>
        Here is what I will tell you plainly. I am sixty. I have lived a good life and I carry a peace most of the people around me do not have. It is not because I am better, smarter, or more disciplined than they are. It is because at some point in the walk, I recognized I could not succeed without surrender. This awareness of the gift of God's grace made me realize it was not something I had to pay back but that I needed to steward it instead. I cannot repay grace. Neither can you. That ledger does not balance. What we can do is hold what we have been given faithfully, and point honestly at where it came from.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is how I see the Voice of Repentance. Not a personality. A record of one man still walking, still learning, still repenting in the real sense of the word, which is to say still turning. Some of what you find here will be written essays. Some will be songs. Some will be chapters of my own story as I put them down. All of it is aimed at the same thing: turning, and inviting you to turn with me.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are willing, start with <a href="/blog/the-resume-that-doesn-t-matter"><em>The Resume That Doesn't Matter</em></a>. Read one post. If the voice makes sense to you, read another. The journey is long, and the first step is just honest reading.
      </p>
    </div>
    </div>

    <aside id="contact" class="lg:sticky lg:top-24 scroll-mt-24">
      <div class="bg-white border border-vor-sand p-8">
      <span class="kicker kicker-muted">Write to Troy</span>
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-vor-charcoal mt-3 mb-4">
        Say what you came to say
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-vor-charcoal-light mb-8">
        This goes to me, and I answer my own mail. Write about something you read,
        something you are carrying, or something you want to ask. If you lead a church or
        a ministry and are writing for that reason, say so below and I will read it in
        that light. Your name and email are kept in my contact records so I can follow up
        and remember the conversation. There is no newsletter here and you will not be
        added to a mailing list.
      </p>

      <form id="write-form" class="space-y-5">
        <div>
          <label for="write-reason" class="block text-sm font-heading font-medium text-vor-charcoal mb-1">
            What is this about?
          </label>
          <select
            id="write-reason"
            name="reason"
            required
            class="w-full px-4 py-3 rounded-lg border border-vor-sand bg-white text-vor-charcoal font-body focus:outline-none focus:border-vor-gold-dark focus:ring-1 focus:ring-vor-gold-dark"
          >
            <option value="" disabled selected>Choose one</option>
            <optgroup label="Personal">
              <option value="post">Something you wrote</option>
              <option value="faith">My own walk, or a question about faith</option>
              <option value="hello">Just reaching out</option>
            </optgroup>
            <optgroup label="Church and ministry leaders">
              <option value="speaking">Speaking or preaching</option>
              <option value="leadership">A ministry leadership question</option>
              <option value="partnership">Working together</option>
            </optgroup>
            <option value="other">Something else</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        <div>
          <label for="write-name" class="block text-sm font-heading font-medium text-vor-charcoal mb-1">Name</label>
          <input
            type="text"
            id="write-name"
            name="name"
            required
            class="w-full px-4 py-3 rounded-lg border border-vor-sand bg-white text-vor-charcoal font-body focus:outline-none focus:border-vor-gold-dark focus:ring-1 focus:ring-vor-gold-dark"
            placeholder="Your name"
          />
        </div>

        <div>
          <label for="write-email" class="block text-sm font-heading font-medium text-vor-charcoal mb-1">Email</label>
          <input
            type="email"
            id="write-email"
            name="email"
            required
            class="w-full px-4 py-3 rounded-lg border border-vor-sand bg-white text-vor-charcoal font-body focus:outline-none focus:border-vor-gold-dark focus:ring-1 focus:ring-vor-gold-dark"
            placeholder="your@email.com"
          />
        </div>

        <!-- Revealed only for the leader reasons, and required once revealed. The
             `required` attribute is toggled in step with visibility: a hidden required
             field blocks submission with an error the visitor cannot see. -->
        <div id="write-leader-fields" class="hidden space-y-5">
          <div>
            <label for="write-organization" class="block text-sm font-heading font-medium text-vor-charcoal mb-1">
              Church or organization
            </label>
            <input
              type="text"
              id="write-organization"
              name="organization"
              class="w-full px-4 py-3 rounded-lg border border-vor-sand bg-white text-vor-charcoal font-body focus:outline-none focus:border-vor-gold-dark focus:ring-1 focus:ring-vor-gold-dark"
              placeholder="Where you serve"
            />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="write-role" class="block text-sm font-heading font-medium text-vor-charcoal mb-1">
              Your role
            </label>
            <input
              type="text"
              id="write-role"
              name="role"
              class="w-full px-4 py-3 rounded-lg border border-vor-sand bg-white text-vor-charcoal font-body focus:outline-none focus:border-vor-gold-dark focus:ring-1 focus:ring-vor-gold-dark"
              placeholder="Pastor, elder, ministry lead"
            />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <label for="write-message" class="block text-sm font-heading font-medium text-vor-charcoal mb-1">Message</label>
          <textarea
            id="write-message"
            name="message"
            rows="6"
            required
            class="w-full px-4 py-3 rounded-lg border border-vor-sand bg-white text-vor-charcoal font-body focus:outline-none focus:border-vor-gold-dark focus:ring-1 focus:ring-vor-gold-dark resize-none"
            placeholder="Take your time."
          ></textarea>
        </div>

        <!-- Honeypot: bots fill this; humans never see it -->
        <input type="text" name="website" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" />
        <div class="cf-turnstile" data-sitekey="0x4AAAAAADvNCYK6GF56tDw4" data-theme="light"></div>

        <button
          type="submit"
          id="write-submit"
          class="w-full px-6 py-3 text-sm font-heading font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-white bg-vor-charcoal rounded-lg hover:bg-vor-charcoal-light transition-colors disabled:opacity-60 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
        >
          Send it
        </button>
        <p class="text-xs text-vor-charcoal-light">
          Your details are kept so Troy can respond and keep track of the conversation.
          Never shared, never sold, never added to a mailing list.
        </p>
      </form>

      <p class="text-sm text-vor-charcoal-light mt-8">
        Asking about AI in ministry specifically? There is a fuller form on
        <a href="/ai-ministry#inquiry" class="underline">AI in ministry</a> that asks the
        right questions for that conversation.
      </p>

      <div id="write-success" class="hidden py-8">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 mb-4 rounded-full bg-vor-warm border border-vor-sand flex items-center justify-center">
          <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-vor-gold-dark" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-heading font-semibold text-vor-charcoal text-lg mb-2">It reached me</h3>
        <p class="text-vor-charcoal-light">I read everything that comes through here. You will hear back.</p>
      </div>

      <div id="write-error" class="hidden py-4 text-red-600 text-sm">
        Something went wrong. Please try again, or email directly at
        <a href="mailto:info@voiceofrepentance.com" class="underline">info@voiceofrepentance.com</a>.
      </div>
      </div>
    </aside>
   </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script is:inline src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js" async defer></script>

<script>
  import { submitForm } from '../lib/formSubmit';

  // Reasons that mean "I am writing as a church or ministry leader". These tag the
  // submission `speaking` so leader mail is filterable, and reveal the optional
  // organization/role fields. Everything else stays `contact`.
  const LEADER_REASONS = new Set(['speaking', 'leadership', 'partnership']);

  const REASON_LABELS: Record<string, string> = {
    post: 'Something you wrote',
    faith: 'My own walk, or a question about faith',
    hello: 'Just reaching out',
    speaking: 'Speaking or preaching',
    leadership: 'A ministry leadership question',
    partnership: 'Working together',
    other: 'Something else',
  };

  const form = document.getElementById('write-form') as HTMLFormElement | null;
  const reasonEl = document.getElementById('write-reason') as HTMLSelectElement | null;
  const leaderFields = document.getElementById('write-leader-fields');
  const submitBtn = document.getElementById('write-submit') as HTMLButtonElement | null;
  const successDiv = document.getElementById('write-success');
  const errorDiv = document.getElementById('write-error');

  const orgEl = document.getElementById('write-organization') as HTMLInputElement | null;
  const roleEl = document.getElementById('write-role') as HTMLInputElement | null;

  // Show and require together. `required` on a hidden input makes the form
  // unsubmittable with a validation message pointing at something invisible.
  function syncLeaderFields() {
    const isLeader = LEADER_REASONS.has(reasonEl?.value || '');
    leaderFields?.classList.toggle('hidden', !isLeader);
    if (orgEl) orgEl.required = isLeader;
    if (roleEl) roleEl.required = isLeader;
  }
  reasonEl?.addEventListener('change', syncLeaderFields);
  syncLeaderFields();

  form?.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    errorDiv?.classList.add('hidden');
    if (submitBtn) {
      submitBtn.disabled = true;
      submitBtn.textContent = 'Sending...';
    }

    const data = new FormData(form);
    const reason = String(data.get('reason') || 'other');
    const isLeader = LEADER_REASONS.has(reason);
    const organization = isLeader ? String(data.get('organization') || '') : '';
    const role = isLeader ? String(data.get('role') || '') : '';

    // Prepend the context to the message so the Telegram ping is readable on its own,
    // the same shape the /ai-ministry form uses.
    const context = [`Reason: ${REASON_LABELS[reason] ?? reason}`];
    if (organization) context.push(`Organization: ${organization}`);
    if (role) context.push(`Role: ${role}`);

    try {
      const res = await submitForm(form, {
        name: String(data.get('name') || ''),
        email: String(data.get('email') || ''),
        organization: organization || null,
        message: `${context.join('\n')}\n\n${String(data.get('message') || '')}`,
        source: isLeader ? 'speaking' : 'contact',
        metadata: { reason, role: role || null },
      });
      if (res.ok) {
        form.classList.add('hidden');
        successDiv?.classList.remove('hidden');
      } else {
        errorDiv?.classList.remove('hidden');
      }
    } catch {
      errorDiv?.classList.remove('hidden');
    } finally {
      if (submitBtn) {
        submitBtn.disabled = false;
        submitBtn.textContent = 'Send it';
      }
    }
  });
</script>
